        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Appliqué embroidered angel, probably from an ecclesiastical vestment. Embroidered on linen grond with gold and silk threads in yellow, green, beige, white and black. Appliqued to wine-colored voided velvet. Cherubim stands on a flaming wheel and holds a scroll. Some silks gone in small areas. Colors bright. Lining and braid later additions."@en ;
